# Line endings.
#
# LF everywhere, including in a Windows working tree. gofmt treats a file with
# CRLF as unformatted, and the Windows CI runner checks out with autocrlf on by
# default, so the first run failed the gofmt step on all 118 files at once.
# Pinning it here fixes that for every machine rather than for the runner alone,
# and it also ends the "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on every commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Captured terminal output, byte for byte.
#
# internal/session/testdata holds real bytes a pseudo-console emitted, escape
# sequences and carriage returns included. The CRs are part of what the terminal
# sent, not line endings: ask_login.bin has 58 of them and the parser under test
# has to cope with exactly that. Normalising these would quietly rewrite the
# evidence and leave the tests passing against a fixture no terminal ever
# produced.
*.bin -text

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
